      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1865 a post office opened, cementing Waterloo as a distinct rural hub amid the valley\u2019s post\u2011Gold Rush wheat and livestock boom.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/waterloo_california",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The historic Cole's Five Cypress Farm, listed on the National Register, showcases 19th\u2011century agricultural heritage at 11221 East Eight Mile Road.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16,
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/waterloo_california",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Waterloo Club, opened in 1984 at 10447 Waterloo Road, is famed for Italian\u2011style barbecue ribs and draws diners from Stockton\u2011Lodi.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
